---
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ADVOCACY } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbSchema, organizationSchema } from '../lib/schema';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Advocacy and system change"
  description="ZeroPlastic campaigns for mandatory Extended Producer Responsibility, an end to single-use PET water bottles in government institutions, and reusable systems."
  image="/images/advocacy-action-800.jpg"
  schema={[
    organizationSchema(),
    breadcrumbSchema([
      { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
      { name: 'Our work', url: '/our-work/' },
      { name: 'Advocacy', url: '/advocacy/' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Advocacy and system change</p>
      <h1>Clean-ups treat the symptom. Policy treats the cause.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        ZeroPlastic is not only a clean-up organisation. Alongside the volunteers on the ground we
        work on behaviour change, policy advocacy and systemic solutions, because every piece of
        plastic on a Sri Lankan beach was a decision made somewhere upstream.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split split--reverse">
        <Figure
          name="advocacy-action"
          alt="ZeroPlastic volunteers in cleaning gloves at a coastal clean-up in Sri Lanka, holding a banner reading Make EPR Mandatory."
          width={2000}
          height={1013}
          sizes="(max-width: 52rem) 100vw, 32rem"
          eager
        />
        <div class="narrative">
          <h2 class="section__title">Three levers, used together</h2>
          <p>
            Behaviour change gets people to refuse plastic. Policy makes refusing it the default.
            Market building puts the alternative within reach at the moment someone needs it.
            Remove any one of the three and the other two stall.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is why our advocacy runs alongside the club network and the clean-ups rather
            than instead of them. The volunteers who fill sacks on a Saturday are the same people
            asking their university, employer or ministry to stop buying the thing they just
            collected.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section__title">What we are campaigning for</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        These are positions we are actively advocating. None of them describes law already in
        force.
      </p>

      <div class="tile-grid">
        {
          ADVOCACY.map((item) => (
            <div class="tile">
              <p class="tile__meta">{item.tag}</p>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p>{item.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="narrative">
          <p class="eyebrow">Campaigning in public</p>
          <h2 class="section__title">Pressure that institutions can see</h2>
          <p>
            Advocacy is not only submissions and meetings. Public campaigns make the case visible,
            bring partners and their teams into the argument, and give institutions a reason to
            move.
          </p>
          <p>
            Campaigns such as PEN BIN Love, which targets the plastic pollution caused by
            disposable pens, show how a specific, everyday product can become the entry point for
            a much wider conversation about single-use plastic.
          </p>
        </div>

        <Figure
          name="advocacy-campaign"
          alt="Campaigners walking with placards reading Stop Pen Pollution and PenBin Love during a ZeroPlastic awareness march."
          width={2000}
          height={1335}
          sizes="(max-width: 52rem) 100vw, 30rem"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-band">
        <div>
          <h2>Work with us on policy</h2>
          <p>
            Institutions, businesses and organisations cutting single-use plastic in their own
            operations are the fastest route to system change. Tell us what you are trying to do.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a class="button button--lg" href="/contact/">Partner With Us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .narrative {
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
</style>
